  "overview": {
    "claims": [
      {
        "attribution": "Richard A. Coad",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "2e9c42eb6cfd922568f786a3e13fce2a1d560c93ef0723da8e9006855e5fc8f7",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-2e9c42eb6cfd-0000-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 3,
              "start": 3
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Richard A. Coad, the case concerns how the federal firearms ban determines which prior convictions count as felonies, with an exemption clause that considers whether a state indicates that a conviction\u2019s civil\u2011rights effects have been removed."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Richard A. Coad",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "2e9c42eb6cfd922568f786a3e13fce2a1d560c93ef0723da8e9006855e5fc8f7",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-2e9c42eb6cfd-0000-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 4,
              "start": 4
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Richard A. Coad, some states, such as Vermont and Maine, do not strip civil rights after convictions, affecting the application of the exemption clause."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Richard A. Coad",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "2e9c42eb6cfd922568f786a3e13fce2a1d560c93ef0723da8e9006855e5fc8f7",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-2e9c42eb6cfd-0000-0004"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 5,
              "start": 5
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Richard A. Coad, restoration of civil rights varies by state; many states automatically restore rights without additional conditions."
      }
    ],
    "heading": "Overview",
    "status": "complete",
    "summary": null,
    "summary_citations": []
  },
  "party_positions": [
    {
      "claims": [
        {
          "attribution": "Richard A. Coad",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "2e9c42eb6cfd922568f786a3e13fce2a1d560c93ef0723da8e9006855e5fc8f7",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-2e9c42eb6cfd-0000-0000"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 3,
                "start": 3
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Richard A. Coad, the petitioner argues that the exemption clause should apply to states where civil rights are never removed, thereby limiting the reach of the firearms ban."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Richard A. Coad",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "2e9c42eb6cfd922568f786a3e13fce2a1d560c93ef0723da8e9006855e5fc8f7",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-2e9c42eb6cfd-0000-0002"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 4,
                "start": 4
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Richard A. Coad, the petitioner points to states such as Vermont and Maine, where civil rights are not taken away, as examples supporting the exemption."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Richard A. Coad",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "2e9c42eb6cfd922568f786a3e13fce2a1d560c93ef0723da8e9006855e5fc8f7",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-2e9c42eb6cfd-0000-0004"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 5,
                "start": 5
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Richard A. Coad, the petitioner notes that many states automatically restore civil rights without further conditions, reinforcing the argument that the exemption should apply broadly."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Richard A. Coad",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "2e9c42eb6cfd922568f786a3e13fce2a1d560c93ef0723da8e9006855e5fc8f7",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-2e9c42eb6cfd-0000-0006"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 15,
                "start": 15
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Richard A. Coad, the petitioner argues that the government\u2019s narrowing of \u201cproblem states\u201d ignores the historical scope of the Armed Career Criminal Act, which looks back to state laws from the 1960s\u20111980s."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Mr. Joseffer",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "2e9c42eb6cfd922568f786a3e13fce2a1d560c93ef0723da8e9006855e5fc8f7",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-2e9c42eb6cfd-0001-0002"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 25,
                "start": 25
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Mr. Joseffer, the petitioner emphasizes that restoring a right does not mean leaving it untouched and that the statute is not absurd."
        }
      ],
